<===> README.md
# Variables of nested imports

A nested import was parsed once and shared by all scopes it was imported
into, but its variable references are cached for the first one (this
crashed). Variables of a nested import were also not visible after the
import, and assignments to root variables didn't create local ones.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> after/child_rule/input.scss
a {@import "n"; c {d: $a}}
<===> after/child_rule/_n.scss
$a: 0;
b {c: $a}
<===> after/child_rule/output.css
a b {
  c: 0;
}
a c {
  d: 0;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> after/import_in_import/input.scss
a {@import "o"}
<===> after/import_in_import/_n.scss
$a: 0;
b {c: $a}
<===> after/import_in_import/_o.scss
@import "n";
d {e: $a}
<===> after/import_in_import/output.css
a b {
  c: 0;
}
a d {
  e: 0;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> after/outer/input.scss
a {$a: 9; @import "q"; d: $a}
<===> after/outer/_q.scss
$a: 1;
<===> after/outer/output.css
a {
  d: 1;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> after/reassign/input.scss
a {@import "n"; $a: 4; d: $a}
<===> after/reassign/_n.scss
$a: 0;
b {c: $a}
<===> after/reassign/output.css
a b {
  c: 0;
}
a {
  d: 4;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> after/twice/input.scss
